  "published": "2026-11-22T08:11:32.93Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v0.1.0 (Initial Release)\n\n\t\t\t• Reversible authentication token issuance and verification engine embedding custom claims using AES-256 authenticated encryption.\n\t\t\t• Key-based AEAD authenticated data encryption using AES-256-GCM with zero-dependency cross-platform fallback for WebAssembly and Server runtimes.\n\t\t\t• API client credential generation, RSA (2048/4096) and ECDSA (P-256) asymmetric key pair creation, PEM export, and digital signing.\n\t\t\t• RFC 6749 and RFC 7519 OAuth2 Bearer access and refresh token generation, HMAC-SHA256 signing, and validation.\n\t\t\t• Deterministic blind indexing via keyed HMAC-SHA256 and HMAC-SHA512 hashing with timing-safe validation.\n\t\t\t• Salted password hashing complying with RFC 2898 PBKDF2-SHA256 with 100,000 iterations.\n\t\t\t• RFC 6238 Time-based One-Time Password (TOTP) two-factor authentication and standard otpauth:// QR URI formatting.\n\t\t\t• Prefixed API key generation and timing-attack-proof SHA-256 validation.\n\t\t\t• Sensitive data masking for credit cards, emails, phone numbers, Aadhaar, SSN/tax IDs, and secret tokens.\n\t\t\t• 1-line DI registration via services.AddDixorSecurity().",
